# The development stack's interpolation file (P1.29). Copy it to deployment/env/dev.env (ignored by git), set the
# values, and keep it mode 0600 and owned by you. `npm run dev:up` passes it as the one --env-file to the preflight and
# to Compose; nothing else reads it, and no service gets it whole. Secrets never go here: they are files in
# deployment/secrets/ (see its README).
#
# `dev` (the homelab) uses the 0x40.space names below; a `local` stack uses *.localhost names instead.

# The web server's own origins (interfaces/http/config.ts): the media origin is another site than the public one, and
# both use a TLD in shared/http/config.ts KNOWN_TLDS, so a local stack uses .test names here, not .localhost.
WEB_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://app.0x40.space
WEB_ALLOWED_HOSTS=app.0x40.space
WEB_MEDIA_ORIGIN=https://media.example.net
